{"id": 19038, "group": "campus-iit-madras-placements", "sent_at": "2026-11-02T13:46:56.127691+00:00", "text": "*Question 1: DSA – Minimum Element Removal* You are given an array of size n. In each iteration, you must: 1. Find the minimum element in the current array. 2. Add this minimum element to the total sum. 3. Delete the minimum element along with its immediate left and right neighbours, if they exist. 4. Repeat the process on the remaining array until it becomes empty. *Return the sum of all the minimum elements selected across all iterations.* ### Example *Input:* text arr = [2, 1, 3, 4, 5] *Explanation:* - *Iteration 1:* The minimum element is 1. Remove 1 and its adjacent elements 2 and 3. The remaining array is [4, 5]. Sum = 1. - *Iteration 2:* The minimum element is 4. Remove 4 and its adjacent element 5. The array becomes empty. Sum = 1 + 4 = 5. *Output:* 5 2.⁠ ⁠It was same across sets, you had to choose one framework among Django, Node.js and Springboot. There was a code base given of an event ticketing platform. ( 50+ files) 6 bugs were defined related to a “promo code” feature. There was documentation about what is the correct way to do several tasks as per the event ticketing platform, however no file paths etc were given. So you had to find the required file with the bug present, and then resolve the bugs. There were 8 tests, and i am guessing some partial marking. No ai assistance", "author_tag": "BHU", "reply_to": {"id": 19036, "text": "ibm qns anyone?", "author_tag": "IITB"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
